From e042eab62fad37ec39da2e673b9a92fb6af080cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritika Chopra <r.chopra@vyos.io>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 20:15:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] T9238: pppoe/disc: drop packets with unsupported PPPoE type
 (port from accel-ppp 315)

The unsupported-PPPoE-type branch in disc_read() logs a warning but
falls through to forward() instead of dropping the packet. Compare
with the unsupported-version branch immediately above, which has the
same shape but continues:

    if (hdr->ver != 1) {
        if (conf_verbose)
            log_warn(...unsupported version...);
        continue;
    }

    if (hdr->type != 1) {
        if (conf_verbose)
            log_warn(...unsupported type...);
        /* falls through into forward() */
    }

Add the missing continue so malformed packets are dropped instead of
processed.

Authored-by: khedor <khedor@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 028e2090389d2b8968dfb30e4d956264718613e5)
---
 accel-pppd/ctrl/pppoe/disc.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/accel-pppd/ctrl/pppoe/disc.c b/accel-pppd/ctrl/pppoe/disc.c
index 17ebd4ec..e5dc942a 100644
--- a/accel-pppd/ctrl/pppoe/disc.c
+++ b/accel-pppd/ctrl/pppoe/disc.c
@@ -363,6 +363,7 @@ static int disc_read(struct triton_md_handler_t *h)
 		if (hdr->type != 1) {
 			if (conf_verbose)
 				log_warn("pppoe: discarding packet (unsupported type %i)\n", hdr->type);
+			continue;
 		}
 
 		if (forward(net, src.sll_ifindex, pack, n))
